Fork notes (markdown-render-speed-02 entry, Agent Lucky)
------------------------------------------------------------
For this entry, marked.esm.js is a performance fork of the file above.
No rendering rule, regular expression, or output string is changed; the
edits only skip work whose outcome is already decided, so the HTML is
byte-for-byte identical to pristine marked 18.1.3 for every input
(verified against the competition's 720 practice cases):

1. Block lexer dispatch (Lexer.blockTokens): before trying the block
   tokenizers, the loop inspects the block's opening characters (after
   at most three leading spaces) and only attempts tokenizers whose
   anchored rules can still match: indented code needs four spaces or
   a tab, fences a backtick or tilde, headings '#', hr '-'/'_'/'*',
   blockquotes '>', lists a bullet or digit, html '<', defs '[', the
   space tokenizer a whitespace-only line start; tables additionally
   need a delimiter row (only '|', ':', '-', spaces, with a '-') as
   the second line, and setext (lheading) underlines are only sought
   before the first blank line. Every guard is a conservative superset
   of the rule it guards: it may pass when the rule then fails, but it
   never fails when the rule would pass, and the original attempt
   order is preserved.

2. Inline lexer dispatch (Lexer inline loop): the same idea per
   position — escape only at a backslash, tag/autolink only at '<',
   link/reflink only at '[' or '![', emStrong only at '*'/'_', codespan
   only at a backtick, br only at a backslash or two spaces, del only
   at '~', and the gfm url tokenizer only when the current word can
   begin a URL or email (starts with www./mailto:/xmpp:, contains an
   '@', or a protocol '://'). In the emphasis masking step, the
   punctuation-masking pass is skipped when the source contains no
   backtick and no backslash (its pattern can only match those), and
   the block-skip pass is skipped when the source contains none of
   '[', backtick, '<' (its alternatives each need one).

3. List tokenizer line scanning (Tokenizer.list): first lines of the
   remaining source and of each item are taken with indexOf/slice
   instead of split(), and the leading-whitespace tab expansion only
   runs on lines that actually begin with a space or tab (the anchored
   pattern it feeds cannot match anything else).

Each edit was verified after application: the entry passes all 720
practice cases byte-for-byte, and renders the corpus faster than the
pristine build.
